## Context

`tests/test_validate.sh` has 36 test cases. `validate_test.go` covers many of
the same broken-header/bad-separator inputs. Per the project's testing policy
(documented in PR #56): Go unit tests own pure-function correctness; shell
tests own CLI black-box behavior.

## Actions

Remove 15 cases from `test_validate.sh` that have direct Go equivalents in
`validate_test.go`. Keep cases that test CLI contracts not covered by Go:
argument parsing, multi-file handling, message text, file-resolution, error
handling, and all forge-ref grammar cases.

## Exit criteria

- `make test-validate` passes with reduced test count
- `make unit-test` still passes (no Go changes)
- Removed cases are all covered by `validate_test.go`
